  "about": "What a pilot's and an airplane's records say, the engine's endorsement_records and inspections_due, which the gateway asks through the planner (POST /api/pilot/endorsements, /api/aircraft/inspections): a solo endorsement good for 90 days (14 CFR 61.87(n), (p)), 61.93(d)(4) and (5) for a solo cross-country, and the inspections in calendar months (91.409(a) and 91.207(d) 12, 91.411(a) and 91.413(a) 24: to the last day of the Nth month after), the 100-hour 100 hours on (91.409(b)) and a VOR check good 30 days within 4 or 6 degrees (91.171). The boundaries: a flight on the 90th day after the endorsement and the day after; an annual on the 5th and on the last day of a month; a check on 29 February. Also the turnaround and the cruise reference (planning_figures) and the E6B's tolerances (workings_right). And AC 61-65K's student endorsements filled in to sign (endorsement_fill, the gateway's EndorsementKind before #482): A.10's words with its blanks filled and no conditions leaving nothing, a blank's spaces closed up and a field it does not take left out; A.8's conditions, which its words lead into, missing; a code no endorsement has is null. dueTone: a paperwork row's tone, past a stop, within 30 days or 10 hours a caution, further off ok (the engine's due_tone).",
